Task 5: Ensemble Learning with Decision Trees and Random Forests

Objective
To master tree-based models, implementing a Decision Tree for interpretability and an Ensemble Random Forest for superior predictive accuracy in classification or regression problems.

Key Outcomes & Skills:
a. Tree Implementation & Visualization: Trained a Decision Tree Classifier and utilized Graphviz to visualize the decision-making structure, demonstrating an understanding of split points and node purity (Entropy/Information Gain).
b. Overfitting Control: Analyzed the risk of overfitting inherent in single Decision Trees and successfully implemented regularization techniques like controlling the tree's depth (max_depth).
c. Ensemble Advantage: Implemented a Random Forest Classifier, showcasing the power of Bagging to reduce variance and significantly improve predictive accuracy over a single Decision Tree.
d. Feature Interpretability: Extracted and interpreted the model's Feature Importance scores from the Random Forest, identifying the most influential predictors to inform business decisions.

Tools and Techniques
    | Category                | Technique/Concept                                                                                           | 
    | :-----------------------| :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------: | 
    | Libraries               | Implementing recommendation algorithms.                                                                     |
    | Concepts                | Decision Trees, Ensemble Learning (Bagging), Overfitting Mitigation, Feature Importance, Cross-Validation.  | 
    | Dataset Used            | Heart Disease Dataset.                                                                                      | 
    
